.TH XWOB 1 "2026" "xwob" "xwob Manual"
.SH NAME
xwob \- overlay volume/backlight/progress bar for Wayland and X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xwob
[\fB\-b\fR \fIbackend\fR] [\fB\-\-print\-backend\fR] [\fIoptions\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xwob
is one command that shows an overlay bar in either kind of session. Inside a
Wayland session it runs the Wayland backend (a fork of wob); inside an X11
session it runs the X11 backend (a fork of xob). Both read values from standard
input, one per line, and draw them on a bar with a percentage label whose text
is black or white depending on what it sits on.
.PP
Standard input and all options after xwob's own are passed to the selected
program unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backend " " \fIauto\fR|\fIwayland\fR|\fIx11\fR
Force a backend. The default is \fIauto\fR (or $XWOB_BACKEND): Wayland when
WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set, otherwise X11 when DISPLAY is set. Use \fIx11\fR on a
Wayland compositor without wlr-layer-shell (for example GNOME) to go through
XWayland.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-backend
Print the backend that would be used and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH INPUT
.TP
.I value
Show the value.
.TP
.IB value !
Use the alternative colours ("alt" style).
.TP
.IB value " " style
(Wayland backend) use a named style from the configuration.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Unless \fB\-c\fR is given, xwob uses
.I ~/.config/xwob/xob.cfg
(X11) or
.I ~/.config/xwob/wob.ini
(Wayland), then the same names under the system configuration directory.
Formats are those of xob (libconfig) and wob (ini); see
.BR xwob\-x11 (1)
and
.BR xwob\-wayland (1).
Both support
.B percentage = true
/
.B show_percentage = yes
to control the label.
.SH SYSTEMD
Install and enable the socket; systemd then starts xwob on the first write:
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user enable --now xwob.socket
systemctl --user import-environment WAYLAND_DISPLAY DISPLAY XAUTHORITY
echo 50 > $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/xwob.sock
.fi
.PP
Stop it with \fBsystemctl --user stop xwob.service\fR (or \fBxwob.socket\fR to
stop listening as well).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xwob\-x11 (1),
.BR xwob\-wayland (1)
